# NOTE: .env is intentionally tracked — it holds ONLY publishable, non-billable
# client-side values (Supabase URL + publishable key). Anything that can be
# SPENT belongs in .env.local and in the host's env vars, even when it is
# technically public: a Google Maps browser key ships in the JS bundle either
# way, but committing it hands it to every scraper that farms AIza prefixes,
# and the bill is yours. Mapbox and Google keys both follow that rule.
